From: RC01 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: serialize group lifetime and locked memory release

Close local review R1/R2 in the 352/914 integration. Initialize QMI work
once at core_alloc, including devices waiting for group partners. Reuse
the existing process-context lifecycle mutex from lookup/assign through
create and from stop through last member removal/list deletion/free.
Workers never acquire it; drop worker-owned ag/core locks across every
cancel/release wait. This serializes rare independent group init/remove.

Stop QMI/recovery on every member before locked DMA/MLO borrower release.
Partial create failure uses the same path after releasing ag/core locks.
Track partial handle/workqueue/power-up ownership and reject late events.
The allocator ABI, firmware profile, ring sizes and HW1 policy stay intact.

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause-Clear
